resources.string:
Cifra Keyboard has no internet permission and sends nothing anywhere: no analytics, no crash reports, no ads.

Only on this device, it keeps:
• your identities: name, public key and the private key sealed by the Android Keystore;
• your contacts: name and public key;
• your ratchet conversations: the keys in use, the keys of messages that have not arrived yet (for up to 7 days) and, if "Read messages again" is on, the keys of messages already read until that time runs out. All of it is sealed by the Android Keystore. While the key of a message exists, that encrypted message can be opened again on this device;
• the keyboard settings and the result of the check in "Key protection on this device".

It never stores your BIP39 words, your passphrase, or the text of the messages you write or decrypt. It reads the clipboard only on this device, to find encrypted messages.

If you turn on the QR code button, the camera is only used while a code is being read: frames are looked at in memory, one at a time, and never stored.

Backups are disabled. "Erase all keys" deletes identities, contacts and conversations; uninstalling the app deletes everything.
